@{ViewData["Title"]="Design system";}
<p class="eyebrow">CIVIC FOUNDATIONS · V1</p><h1>One service. A consistent experience.</h1><p class="lede">Tokens, patterns, content guidance, and governance connect our components to the people using them.</p><div class="detail-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Foundations</h2><p>Semantic HTML provides the structure. Shared Sass tokens define color, spacing, typography, and visible focus. Plain language makes decisions easier.</p><span class="badge">Submitted</span><p><a class="button" asp-action="Create">Primary action</a></p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Framework versus system</h2><p>Bootstrap supplies utilities and components. Material defines interaction and visual patterns. An enterprise design system adds service principles, accessibility rules, approved content, ownership, versioning, and review.</p><p>This portal uses native components with shared tokens. Framework adapters live in the frontend package.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Component contract</h2><p>Every field has a visible label, every action a clear name, and every status a text equivalent. Validation appears in a focusable summary. Navigation and tables retain semantic structure.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Change governance</h2><p>Propose a user need, review the design, test with keyboard and assistive technology, document evidence, and release a versioned change. Designers and developers share acceptance criteria.</p></section></div>

@section Styles {<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/frameworks.css">}
@section Scripts {<script type="module" src="~/js/framework-components.js"></script>}
<section class="panel"><h2>Framework adapters</h2><p>Bootstrap and Material components use the Civic Foundations primary color token.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/Home/Index">Bootstrap case list</a><md-filled-button href="/Home/Index">Material case list</md-filled-button></div></section>
